<description>
Paint a recolored diagonal copy from each L triomino source object.

Input structure:
- The background is the dominant color.
- The only foreground objects are 4-connected red and grey L triominoes,
  each occupying three pixels of a 2x2 box.

Rule:
- Grey L objects paint a yellow copy translated one diagonal step toward
  their missing 2x2 corner.
- Red L objects paint a green copy translated one diagonal step away from
  their missing 2x2 corner.
- Copies are clipped by the grid boundary; red-derived green copies are
  painted after grey-derived yellow copies where the projections collide.

Key insight:
- The missing corner of each 2x2 L object identifies its diagonal axis, and
  the source color determines which side of that axis receives the copy.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_along_path",
  "src": "red and grey 4-connected L-triomino objects",
  "path": "one diagonal step along the missing-corner axis; grey moves toward the missing corner, red moves away from it",
  "trajectory": "paint one clipped copy of the L object",
  "transform": "grey copy -> yellow; red copy -> green; keep source objects unchanged",
  "notes": "red-derived green copy covers grey-derived yellow copy on collisions"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 8-16 rows x 8-16 cols, square [observed]
  background: orange (7)
  objects:
    type: L-triominoes (3 cells of a 2x2 box, one corner missing)
    colors: exactly red (2) and grey (5); >=1 of each
    count: 3-16 total; scales with grid area (~0.14-0.19 density ratio = 3*count / area)
    orientation: all 4 missing-corner positions allowed
  placement_constraints:
    - each copy destination (3 diag-offset cells) must land on background (not on any source object)
    - same-color copies must not overlap each other
    - cross-color copy overlap is allowed (green paints over yellow)
    - boundary clipping of copies is allowed (0-2 cells may be out of bounds)
  transform:
    grey_copy: translate 1 diagonal step TOWARD missing corner, recolor yellow (4)
    red_copy: translate 1 diagonal step AWAY from missing corner, recolor green (3)
    paint_order: yellow first, then green (green wins on overlap)
    source objects preserved in output

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick grid size H=W from [8,10,12,14,16].
    2. Choose object count N (3-16) proportional to area; pick red/grey split with >=1 each.
    3. For each object, pick a random L orientation (missing corner) and source color.
       Compute the copy offset (grey=toward, red=away).
    4. Place objects one at a time. For each, pick a random position and verify:
       a. The 2x2 source bbox fits in grid
       b. All 3 source cells are on background
       c. All in-bounds copy cells (up to 3) are on background and not occupied by prior source/copy cells
       Mark both source and copy cells as occupied.
    5. Derive input by keeping only source cells (remove yellow/green copy cells).
```
